The issue missed here is the case of something like:

```html
<script type="importmap">
{
  "scopes": {
    "/": {
      "/app.js": "/app-dev.js"
    }
  }
}
</script>
<script type="module">
import '//app.js';
</script>
<script type="importmap">
{
  "scopes": {
    "/": {
      "/app.js": "/app-notdev.js"
    }
  }
}
</script>
<script type="module">
import '/app.js';
</script>
```

allowing the interpretation of the `app.js` URL import to change, when it should probably be skipped.

On the other hand, changing the first `<script type="module">` to use `import '/app.js'` instead passes the check that `specifierKey is a code unit prefix of record's span`, which seems inconsistent to me.

The fix would be to check `asURL` instead of `specifierKey` something like:

```suggestion
            <ol>
             <li><p><var>specifierKey</var> ends with U+002F (/).</p></li>

             <li><p>Either <var>specifierKey</var> is a <span>code unit prefix</span> of
             either <var>record</var>'s <span
             data-x="specifier-resolution-record-specifier">specifier</span> or <span
             data-x="specifier-resolution-record-as-url">asURL</span>.</p></li>

             <li><p>Either <var>record</var>'s <span
             data-x="specifier-resolution-record-as-url">asURL</span> is null or <span>is
             special</span></p></li>
            </ol>
```

My preference would still be to ban always disabling shadowing these URLs, as opposed to landing this fix per the previous discussion.
